        "title": "Product and Price",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Two of the four Ps, joined because they are the most *quantitative* and the most\n*coupled*: what you build (product) sets what you can charge (price), and price\nfeeds back into what's worth building. The landscape runs from defining the\noffering, through its life cycle, to setting the number on the tag."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-PRODUCT-AND-PRICE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-PRODUCT-AND-PRICE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:04-product-and-price, git-history:marketing:04-product-and-price]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/04-PRODUCT-AND-PRICE.md",
        "concepts": "[product life cycle, new product development, pricing, price elasticity, value-based pricing]",
        "current_path": "marketing/04-PRODUCT-AND-PRICE.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:product-and-price",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[pricing, product life cycle]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Product and Price",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                      PRODUCT + PRICE LANDSCAPE                          |\n|                                                                         |\n|  PRODUCT SIDE                          PRICE SIDE                       |\n|  ------------                          ----------                       |\n|  What is the offering?                 What does the buyer pay?         |\n|                                                                         |\n|  .------------------.                  .------------------------.       |\n|  | PRODUCT LEVELS   |                  | PRICING APPROACH       |       |\n|  | core->actual->   |                  | cost+ / competition /  |       |\n|  |  augmented       |                  | VALUE-BASED            |       |\n|  '------------------'                  '------------------------'       |\n|         |                                       |                       |\n|         v                                       v                       |\n|  .------------------.                  .------------------------.       |\n|  | LIFE CYCLE       |  --- price ----> | ELASTICITY of demand   |       |\n|  | intro->growth->  |    moves with    | how volume responds    |       |\n|  |  maturity->decline    the stage     | to a price change      |       |\n|  '------------------'                  '------------------------'       |\n|         |                                       |                       |\n|         v                                       v                       |\n|  .------------------.                  .------------------------.       |\n|  | NEW-PRODUCT DEV  |                  | PRICE STRUCTURE        |       |\n|  | idea->...->launch|                  | tiers, bundles, discr. |       |\n|  '------------------'                  '------------------------'       |\n|                                                                         |\n|  Price is the ONLY P that directly produces revenue; the rest cost.     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
