        "title": "Product and Price",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Price is special: **Product, Place, and Promotion are cost centers; Price is the\nrevenue lever.** A 1% price improvement typically moves profit more than a 1% cost\ncut, because it flows straight to the bottom line. This guide draws on\n`economics/01-MICROECONOMICS.md` for demand/elasticity theory and applies it."
    },
